<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
  <section xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-01-project-design">
    <title>Project Design</title>
    <introduction>
    <p>Before we get started, let's talk about the project design.</p>
    <p>We are making a game that has 3 physical elements, 1. A ship that 
        is propelled by rocket power, 2. A lasso that is launched from the
        ship, grows, and collects crystals, and 3. A crystal that grows and
        has 3 different growth states shown with different artwork.
    </p>
    <figure>
        <caption>Space Farm Parts</caption>
        <sidebyside>
    <figure>
      <caption>Farming Spaceship</caption>
      <image source="farm-space-ship.webp" width="75%" >
         <shortdescription>A spaceship with a rocket tail.</shortdescription>
     </image>
      </figure>
      <figure>
      <caption>Farming Lasso</caption>
      <image source="farm-lasso.webp" width="75%" >
         <shortdescription>A blue ring.</shortdescription>
     </image>
      </figure>
      <figure>
      <caption>Farming Crystal</caption>
      <image source="farm-crystal.webp" width="75%" >
         <shortdescription>A purple crystal.</shortdescription>
     </image>
      </figure>
    </sidebyside>
</figure>
    <p>Both the lasso, and the crystal will inherit the 
        GrowingArea2D class that we make.
    </p>
    <p>The hierarchy of scenes will look like this.</p>
    <figure xml:id="space-farm-class-hierarchy">
      <caption>Scene Hierarchy</caption>
      <image source="space-farm-growing-area-hierarchy.webp" width="75%" >
         <shortdescription>The project folder view is shown with default files.</shortdescription>
     </image>
      </figure>
    <p>The GrowingArea2D has parameters to decide behavior
        of the growth. First it has a starting scale and and maximum scale.
        Then it has a growth rate and an optional growth curve for the growth rate.
        Then it has settings for whether it should automatically start growing on
        creation and if when it gets to the maximum size it should be removed from the
        scene. The last three parameters are an array of size thresholds so that behavior 
        can change based on different stages of growth, the current_scale, and whether or
        not the area is currently growning.
    </p>
    <p>There are also 2 signals. One for indicating that the maximum size was reached,
        and the other for the size changing.
    </p>

    
    </introduction>
    <subsection xml:id="two-d-games-space-farm-scenes">
      <title>Organizing the project</title>
      <p>In this project, we will make 4 independent scenes: <c>Player</c>, <c>Collector</c>, 
                <c>Prize</c>, and <c>HUD</c>, which we will combine into the game's <c>Main</c> scene, and
            the <c>Collector</c> and <c>Prize</c> scenes will inherit from the <c>GrowingArea</c> scene.</p>
      
      <p>We are using pretty simple artwork. 1 image for the ship, and 3 images for the
        3 sizes of crystal. The lasso of the collector and flame for the rocket of the ship
         will be drawn programmatically.
      </p>
      </subsection>
    </section>
